Here is the plan for the two bugs:

---

## Bug 1 – Auto-create pending evaluations on course creation

**File**: [`backend/app/Http/Controllers/StudentClassController.php`](backend/app/Http/Controllers/StudentClassController.php)

**Root cause**: `store()` creates `ClassSession` rows (lines 279–318) but never creates `LearningRecord` rows. The Learning Records page only reads existing database rows, so a new course has nothing to show.

**Fix**: After `ClassSession::insert($sessions)` (line 317), loop over `$sessions` and bulk-insert one `LearningRecord` per session with `Status = 'pending'`. Required fields (`StudentClassID`, `TeacherID`, `Subject`, `SessionDate`, `StartTime`, `EndTime`, `Status`, `Content`) are all already available in the `$sessions` array and `$data`. `ClassSessionID` will be left null since bulk insert does not return individual IDs (nullable already allowed).

---

## Bug 2 – "全部" mode always shows Week 1, hiding courses starting mid-month

**File**: [`frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue`](frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue), line 670

**Root cause**: `const weekNum = displayWeek.value || 1` — when `displayWeek === 0` ("全部"), the calendar is permanently anchored to Week 1. A course with `first_class_date = '2026-02-09'` (Monday) only becomes visible starting Week 3, but the user never knows to navigate there.

**Fix**: Add a `currentDisplayWeek()` helper that returns the week-of-month number containing today's date (when the displayed month = current month), or 1 otherwise. Use it in `getDisplayDateFull`:

```js
const currentDisplayWeek = () => {
  const today = new Date();
  if (today.getFullYear() !== displayYear.value || today.getMonth() + 1 !== displayMonth.value) return 1;
  const todayStr = today.toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  for (let w = 1; w <= 5; w++) {
    const mon = getMondayOfMonthWeek(displayYear.value, displayMonth.value, w);
    const sun = addDays(mon, 6);
    if (todayStr >= mon && todayStr <= sun) return w;
  }
  return 1;
};

const getDisplayDateFull = (dayOfWeek) => {
  const weekNum = displayWeek.value === 0 ? currentDisplayWeek() : displayWeek.value;
  // ... rest unchanged ...
};
```

This makes the default "全部" view open on today's week for the current month, so a course starting this week (or any nearby week reachable via 上週/下週) is immediately visible.

---

## Deployment

`npm run deploy` in `frontend/` after both fixes. No database migration needed.

---

